diff --git a/docs/src/man/man1/halui.1.adoc b/docs/src/man/man1/halui.1.adoc
index c172f579cd..003290e96a 100644
--- a/docs/src/man/man1/halui.1.adoc
+++ b/docs/src/man/man1/halui.1.adoc
@@ -371,6 +371,34 @@ _L_ = axis letter (xyzabcuvw)
 *halui.axis.selected.plus* bit in::
   pin for jogging the selected axis bit in in positive direction at the halui.axis.jog-speed velocity
 
+=== Power Feed Jogging
+
+These inputs exist only with '[DISPLAY] LATHE = true' and configured X/Z axes.
+Power-feed directions use separate inputs from ordinary axis jogging.
+
+*halui.power-feed.x.plus/minus* bit in (default: *FALSE*)::
+  Request spindle-dependent power feed in the positive/negative X direction.
+*halui.power-feed.z.plus/minus* bit in (default: *FALSE*)::
+  Request spindle-dependent power feed in the positive/negative Z direction.
+*halui.power-feed.per-rev* float in (default: *0*)::
+  Positive physical machine units/revolution, captured on the first press until
+  all X/Z buttons release. Interpreter F and G95 are not consulted.
+*halui.power-feed.spindle* u32 in (default: *0*)::
+  Configured spindle index. Speed uses the absolute speed-in feedback in
+  revolutions/second; feed override remains live and is applied once.
+*halui.power-feed.taper-slope* float in (default: *0*)::
+  Finite physical delta-X/delta-Z in [-1,1]. Zero disables taper. For slope k,
+  Z+ moves along (k,1)
+  and X+ along (1,-k), normalized to preserve the requested path feedrate.
+  Simultaneous X/Z inputs combine before normalization. Diameter mode has no
+  effect on this physical slope.
+
+The coupled axes share one acceleration/limit-constrained path. Direction
+changes decelerate before changing that path. A stop of either axis stops both.
+Spindle or taper changes while held require neutral before rearming.
+Power feed requires enabled, homed manual teleop motion and a commanded-on,
+available spindle. It is speed-based feed, not synchronized threading.
+
 === Flood coolant
 
 *halui.flood.is-on* bit out::
